[0.003, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[4A\r\u001b[J\r\nBoth parts are done, and the suite passes with 8 tests.\r\n\r\n\u001b[2m- \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36mmode()\u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u001b[0m\u001b[1min\u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36mstats.py\u001b[0m\u001b[1m:\u001b[0m Returns the most frequent value. On a tie it returns the smallest tied value,\r\n  and it raises \u001b[36mValueError\u001b[0m on empty input. Four tests in \u001b[36mtest_stats.py\u001b[0m cover a clear mode, a tie, a\r\n  single value, and the empty case.\r\n\u001b[2m- \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36mREADME.md\u001b[0m\u001b[1m:\u001b[0m Covers the four functions, their edge cases, a usage example, and the test command.\r\n\r\nTwo things to know:\r\n\r\n\u001b[2m- \u001b[0mThe \u001b[36mmedian\u001b[0m fix from earlier is still uncommitted, so \u001b[36mgit\u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[36mdiff\u001b[0m shows it alongside \u001b[36mmode()\u001b[0m.\r\n\u001b[2m- \u001b[0mThe README's usage example is not run by any test, and I checked it by reading only. Its values\r\n  (\u001b[36mmean\u001b[0m 2.8, \u001b[36mmedian\u001b[0m 3, \u001b[36mspread\u001b[0m 4, \u001b[36mmode\u001b[0m 1) are correct for \u001b[36m[3,\u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[36m1,\u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[36m4,\u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[36m1,\u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[36m5]\u001b[0m.\r\n\r\nNothing is committed.\r\n\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500"]
